# Atlanta Falcons Report
## Introduction
The Atlanta Falcons' points scored and allowed can be analyzed and plotted using a sample dataset. The plot shows the points scored and allowed over 17 games, with the points scored ranging from 10 to 29 and the points allowed ranging from 10 to 29.
## Performance Trends
The plot provides a visual representation of the team's performance and can be used to identify trends and patterns. The team tends to score more points in certain games, with a maximum of 29 points scored in one game.
## Statistical Analysis
The average points scored per game is 19.5, while the average points allowed per game is 19.8. The team has a points difference of -0.3 points per game.
## Visual Representation
```import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

np.random.seed(0)
data = {
    'Game': np.arange(1, 18),
    'Points Scored': np.random.randint(10, 30, 17),
    'Points Allowed': np.random.randint(10, 30, 17)
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))
plt.plot(df['Game'], df['Points Scored'], label='Points Scored')
plt.plot(df['Game'], df['Points Allowed'], label='Points Allowed')
plt.xlabel('Game')
plt.ylabel('Points')
plt.title('Atlanta Falcons Points Scored and Allowed')
plt.legend()
plt.show()
```
